    <h1>
        Understand the engine.
        <br />
        <span class="docs-accent">Build with its SDK.</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        This documentation describes the Crafty implementation in the repository: its runtime, ECS, world storage, chunk pipeline, renderer, UI, and the public SDK contracts available to mod authors.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-warning">
        <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle"></i>
        <div>
            <strong>Repository snapshot and implementation status</strong>
            <p>
                These pages are based on the repository source, not assumptions about planned features. In this snapshot, external mod assembly loading and the MDK are not implemented. The built-in content mod is initialized directly by the game. See
                <a href="/docs/lifecycle">Mod Loading Status</a>
                before planning a distributable mod.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2>What Crafty is made of</h2>

    <p>
        Crafty is a data-oriented voxel game written in C# on .NET 10. The repository contains the game, its custom runtime, the public SDK, and the world/chunk generation library. Vulcan is the low-level graphics foundation, but its source is maintained outside this repository and is referenced through machine-specific project paths.
    </p>

